        answer_en: "**The Appearance Panel in V3 is the undisputed secret weapon for building hyper-complex Graphic Styles on a single, clean vector path!**\n\nConventionally, a vector object is limited to one solid Fill and one continuous Stroke. The Appearance Panel completely shatters this limitation:\n- **Infinite Stroke Stacking:** You can literally assign a single line of text a 20px solid black outer stroke, a 10px white stroke layered inside that, and a 2px glowing dashed stroke on top—all governed by one physical object!\n- **Multiple Fill Layers:** You can establish a solid base color fill, and stack a 50% opacity radial gradient fill directly on top of it, managing both independently.\n- **Micro-Blend Modes:** Every single stroke or fill assigned in this panel can have its own independent Opacity and Blend Mode (e.g., setting a specific inner stroke to 'Overlay' without affecting the base fill).\n\n💡 **The Greatest Benefit:** Extreme layer economy! Instead of duplicating a text layer 5 times to create a retro multi-stroked typography effect, you manage it all on one editable text string. If the client changes the wording, the massive stack of dynamic strokes immediately updates!",
